# Studio local development — the one file, and this is what it looks like.
# Real file: ~/.config/andreas-services/studio/dev.env (or $STUDIO_DEV_ENV_FILE).
# Not committed; outside the repo so it survives git clean, is shared by every
# worktree on the machine, and holds secrets where no `git add -f` reaches them.
#
# Readers: dev-setup.sh writes the generated section from this machine's dev
# stack; dev-up.sh exports only VITE_* before Vite starts and reads the token
# for the local API; the pipeline reads it through `env_value`; dev-user.sh and
# dev-token.sh read the account. The deployed half never sees it.
#
# Which STACK a command targets is NOT here — that is a profile:
# `studio profile show`, `studio --profile prod <command>`. STUDIO_S3_BUCKET and
# STUDIO_CATALOG_TABLE lines are dropped on import for that reason.

# ---- generated (rewritten on every dev-setup.sh run; do not hand-edit) --------

# Frontend (Vite inlines VITE_*; dev-up.sh exports only this prefix). The DEV
# Cognito pool and its Managed Login host — local development never signs in
# against production. VITE_API_URL stays on localhost: dev-up.sh runs the API here.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_example
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=example
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=studio-dev-000000000000.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com

# ---- yours (kept as-is across reruns) -----------------------------------------

# Dev test account — dev-user.sh writes both; a reserved .test address belongs here.
STUDIO_DEV_USER_EMAIL=dev@studio.test
STUDIO_DEV_USER_PASSWORD=

# Provider tokens for the LOCAL pipeline; the deployed half never sees them.
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN is required for every generation (https://replicate.com/account/api-tokens).
# Assets are never uploaded to Replicate — only presigned S3 URLs reach a model.
#REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=
